# SatQuery AI — Model 1: Remote Sensing VQA (Optical + SAR)

A single, self-contained Google Colab notebook that **auto-collects data, fine-tunes a VLM, evaluates, and saves everything to Google Drive**.

---

## Goal

Build a prototype VQA model that:
1. Accepts a **single remote-sensing image** (Optical OR SAR) + a natural-language question.
2. Returns a **generative, free-form natural-language answer** (not classification).
3. Trains on a small curated dataset of **~200 images** (100 Optical + 100 SAR).
4. Runs end-to-end on a **Google Colab T4 GPU** within a single session.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Model Choice:** I recommend **BLIP-2 with OPT-2.7B** (`Salesforce/blip2-opt-2.7b`), loaded in **4-bit quantization** and fine-tuned with **LoRA adapters**. This model natively supports image+text → text generation (VQA) and fits on a T4 GPU (16 GB VRAM). Alternatives considered:
> - *LLaVA-1.5-7B*: Better quality but tight on T4 memory.
> - *PaliGemma-3B*: Good but requires HuggingFace access approval.
> - *Florence-2*: Very small but weaker at open-ended generation.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dataset Source for SAR:** Getting SAR images with labels programmatically in Colab is non-trivial. The planned approach is:
> - **Primary**: Use **BigEarthNet-MM** (both S1/SAR and S2/Optical with shared multi-labels) via HuggingFace streaming — download ONLY ~100 patches per modality, not the full 60 GB archive.
> - **Fallback**: Use **EuroSAT** from HuggingFace for optical + download SAR patches from the BigEarthNet Zenodo archive via targeted HTTP range requests.
> - **Last resort**: Use **EuroSAT** for optical and synthesize SAR-like images (single-channel + speckle noise) for the prototype proof-of-concept.

